  "paper": "special-relativity",
  "argument": "arg-sr-charge-current",
  "title": "Charge density depends on the frame",
  "spoken": "Primed charge density is gamma times rho minus v J x over c squared.",
  "explanation": "A current in one system contributes to the charge density in the other. A wire that is neutral in the stationary system but carries a current is not neutral in the moving system.",
  "review": "draft",
  "notation": "modern-pedagogical",
  "unitSystem": "si",
  "assumptions": [
    "The moving system moves along x at speed v relative to the stationary system, with |v| < c. Modern teaching notation: gamma is the paper's beta, c its V.",
    "Charge density and the current along x transform together; the currents across the motion are unchanged by this boost."
  ],
